    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 📄 PDF Compressor\n",
        "\n",
        "Compress multiple PDF files using Ghostscript directly in Google Colab.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Features\n",
        "- Upload multiple PDF files at once\n",
        "- Choose Low, Medium, or High compression\n",
        "- Process all PDFs automatically\n",
        "- Show original and compressed file sizes\n",
        "- Calculate compression percentage\n",
        "- Create one ZIP containing all compressed PDFs\n",
        "- Automatically download the ZIP file\n",
        "\n",
        "### Compression levels\n",
        "- 🟢 **Low** — better quality, larger file\n",
        "- 🟡 **Medium** — balanced quality and file size\n",
        "- 🔴 **High** — smaller file, lower image quality"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Install Ghostscript"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!apt-get update -qq\n",
        "!apt-get install -y -qq ghostscript"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Upload Multiple PDF Files\n",
        "\n",
        "Select one or multiple PDF files from your computer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from google.colab import files\n",
        "\n",
        "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
        "\n",
        "pdf_files = [\n",
        "    filename\n",
        "    for filename in uploaded.keys()\n",
        "    if filename.lower().endswith('.pdf')\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Uploaded {len(pdf_files)} PDF file(s):\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for pdf_file in pdf_files:\n",
        "    print(f\"  - {pdf_file}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Select Compression Level\n",
        "\n",
        "Change `COMPRESSION_LEVEL` to one of:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "low\n",
        "medium\n",
        "high\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "**Low** keeps better image quality. **High** produces smaller files but may reduce image quality."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "COMPRESSION_LEVEL = 'medium'\n",
        "\n",
        "compression_settings = {\n",
        "    'low': '/printer',\n",
        "    'medium': '/ebook',\n",
        "    'high': '/screen'\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "if COMPRESSION_LEVEL not in compression_settings:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"COMPRESSION_LEVEL must be 'low', 'medium', or 'high'\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "ghostscript_setting = compression_settings[COMPRESSION_LEVEL]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Selected compression: {COMPRESSION_LEVEL.upper()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Ghostscript preset: {ghostscript_setting}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Compress PDFs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "import subprocess\n",
        "\n",
        "output_folder = 'compressed_pdfs'\n",
        "os.makedirs(output_folder, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "compressed_files = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for pdf_file in pdf_files:\n",
        "    base_name = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(pdf_file))[0]\n        "    output_file = os.path.join(\n",
        "        output_folder,\n",
        "        f'{base_name}_compressed.pdf'\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f'Compressing: {pdf_file}')\n",
        "\n",
        "    command = [\n",
        "        'gs',\n",
        "        '-sDEVICE=pdfwrite',\n",
        "        '-dCompatibilityLevel=1.4',\n",
        "        f'-dPDFSETTINGS={ghostscript_setting}',\n",
        "        '-dNOPAUSE',\n",
        "        '-dQUIET',\n",
        "        '-dBATCH',\n",
        "        f'-sOutputFile={output_file}',\n",
        "        pdf_file\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        subprocess.run(\n",
        "            command,\n",
        "            check=True,\n",
        "            stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n",
        "            stderr=subprocess.PIPE\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        if os.path.exists(output_file):\n",
        "            original_size = os.path.getsize(pdf_file)\n",
        "            compressed_size = os.path.getsize(output_file)\n",
        "\n",
        "            reduction = (\n",
        "                1 - compressed_size / original_size\n",
        "            ) * 100\n",
        "\n",
        "            compressed_files.append(output_file)\n",
        "\n",
        "            print(f'  ✓ Saved: {output_file}')\n",
        "            print(\n        "                f'  Original:   {original_size / 1024 / 1024:.2f} MB'\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            print(\n        "                f'  Compressed: {compressed_size / 1024 / 1024:.2f} MB'\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            print(f'  Reduction:  {reduction:.1f}%\\n')\n",
        "\n",
        "    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n",
        "        print(f'  ✗ Failed: {pdf_file}')\n",
        "        print(e.stderr.decode('utf-8', errors='ignore'))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f'Finished. Compressed {len(compressed_files)} PDF file(s).')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Create ZIP File"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import zipfile\n",
        "\n",
        "zip_name = f'compressed_pdfs_{COMPRESSION_LEVEL}.zip'\n",
        "\n",
        "with zipfile.ZipFile(\n",
        "    zip_name,\n",
        "    'w',\n",
        "    zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED\n",
        ") as zipf:\n",
        "    for compressed_file in compressed_files:\n",
        "        zipf.write(\n",
        "            compressed_file,\n",
        "            arcname=os.path.basename(compressed_file)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f'✓ Created: {zip_name}')\n",
        "print(f'✓ Contains {len(compressed_files)} PDF file(s)')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Download Automatically"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from google.colab import files\n",
        "\n",
        "if compressed_files:\n",
        "    files.download(zip_name)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('No compressed PDF files available for download.')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📊 Compression Levels\n",
        "\n",
        "| Level | Quality | File Size | Best For |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| 🟢 Low | High | Larger | Printing / high quality |\n",
        "| 🟡 Medium | Good | Medium | General use |\n",
        "| 🔴 High | Lower | Smaller | Email / web / storage |\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Note:** Actual file-size reduction depends heavily on the contents of the PDF. PDFs containing already-compressed images or mostly vector/text content may not become much smaller."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
